From 268ea28739c94321ef9d5407b91a69cbb2575906 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:52:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 42/51] coh: lean sampling (build 76): no TSC in unsampled
 sections; per-thread port counters

Instrumentation (observation only, no protocol change):
- Counts exact in every section; every duration only in timed sections:
  a jittered 1-in-N countdown for read sections and, separately, for
  write sections (write_sampled -> ThreadAnchor.reserved[0]); estimators
  x * read_sections / check_sampled and x * write_sections / write_sampled.
- Unsampled sections read no TSC and add no thread-local lookups outside
  the API entry: c3.cc seqlock hooks and the KV Get stage/copy markers use
  ReadHandle/WriteHandle fields; NR anchors are timed through a separate FFI
  entry GetAnchorTimed (one shared execute_anchor copy, no TLS read inside
  the measured lookup); spin, NR-wait and reclaim sites count always and
  time only while the thread's section-timed flag is set (waitstat slot 6).
- MEGALON_COH_EVENTS=always (validation): read events and all writes timed
  in every section; CohSnap.reserved[1] = bit0 timers | bit1 lean | bit2
  events_always.
- KV create counts no longer depend on the timers (kvw_copied bool).
Port fix (not instrumentation): ObjectStore's process-wide counter atomics
(one locked add per read section, three per write section, on lines shared
by all threads) become per-thread blocks summed by Stats().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
